<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia Oct manufacturing output prices up.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia Oct manufacturing output prices up.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's manufacturing output prices rose 0.2 percent in October to be 0.8 percent up on the year, the Australian Bureau of Statistics reported on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Manufacturing output prices (base 1988/89):</p>
<p>				    Index   mth/mth pct  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    October		     121.4     +0.2	 +0.8</p>
<p>    September		   121.1     +0.1	 +0.5</p>
<p>    October 1995		120.4     -0.1	 +3.1</p>
<p>Note - The bureau said a sharp rise in petroleum prices was the main cause of the increase in October, although it was partly offset by falls in prices of basic metal products and motor vehicles.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
